course: dictionary
lesson: 10989
title: Warriors, old and new
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A warrior is a brave fighter or soldier. The words around it give you clues. «Attila led the Huns, horse-riding warriors from the east, and attacked both halves of the empire.» Led and attacked tell you the warriors were fighters in battle.
explain: Warrior can also mean someone who fights hard for a cause or keeps going through difficult things. «Valhalla, the hall of fallen warriors» is a place in Viking myths, and fallen is a clue that these warriors had died in battle.
explain: Always test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Goliath was a giant Philistine warrior who challenged Israel's army.» Put fighter in place of warrior: Goliath was a giant Philistine fighter who challenged Israel's army. It still makes sense, so fighter is a good match.
fact: Warrior is a noun. One warrior, many warriors.
fact: «Warrior» means a brave fighter or soldier, especially in old times or in stories.
fact: «Warrior» can also mean someone who fights hard for a cause, like an eco-warrior.
fact: «Brave warrior» and «warrior queen» are phrases you may see in stories and history.
fact: «Weekend warrior» is an informal phrase, so do not use it in formal writing.
exercise: In «Attila led the Huns, horse-riding warriors from the east», what does warriors mean? | *Brave fighters | Farmers who grow grain | Traders who sell silk | Teachers
exercise: Which word means the same as warrior in «Goliath was a giant Philistine warrior»? | Baker | Gardener | *Fighter | Singer
exercise: Maya joins a group that fights hard to save the rainforest. She is an eco-warrior. What does warrior suggest here? | *Someone who fights hard for a cause | A cook | A sleepy person | A soldier from long ago
test: In Viking myths, «Valhalla, the hall of fallen warriors» is a place for which people? | *Brave fighters who died in battle | Sailors on holiday | Singers | Shopkeepers
test: What is the plural of warrior? | *warriors | warriores | warrioren | warrior's
exam: Which example shows warrior meaning someone who keeps fighting hard through difficulty? | *A brave child, called a little warrior, fights a long illness | «Valhalla, the hall of fallen warriors» | «Goliath was a giant Philistine warrior»
